# Confinement judged by the 8 neighbours sees a nook but not a dead-end region a few cells deep. A persistent ROOM channel — known free space blurred over the map, kept between thoughts — measures how open the region around each cell is, so sources and frontier marks inside pockets and corridors fade while those in open country (where more food and more frontier lie beyond) win. The agent commits to open regions and stops being pulled into dead pockets.

channel source
channel solid
channel free
channel thing
channel here
channel value
channel room: init 0
channel injection

# Regional openness: known-free space, diffused over the map and remembered.
rule openness:
  when 1
  set room = clamp(0.6 * avg8(room) + 0.4 * free * (1 - solid), 0, 1)

# A source counts in proportion to how open its region is.
rule inject:
  when 1
  set injection = max(thing, source) * (0.3 + 0.7 * room)

# The Bellman wave over the weighted sources.
rule wave:
  when 1
  set value = max(injection, max(0.94 * max4(value), 0.916214 * max8(value))) * (1 - solid * (1 - leak))
